  "scope": "Assistant-bound local templates support exact variable labels and hints, required/optional values, literal defaults and bounded choices. Explicit insertion selects the linked existing assistant in the same draft update, retaining attachments and context without sending a model request. Transactional saving rejects a deleted assistant without partial template changes; deleting an assistant clears only that binding. Unit checks cover real filesystem atomic failure/retry, complete backup restoration and prototype-safe rendering. Four native checks cover actual editor keyboard input, cancellation, literal preview, insertion, stale-assistant rejection/retry, dark minimum-window zoom/focus/Escape, real gzip export/import and normal restart. All 638 unit checks and 210 source desktop checks pass with normal close; five current full-run captures were individually reviewed. Earlier selector, restart-fixture, record-writer and screenshot-paint failures remain archived as negative evidence. Native picker and confirmation responses are isolated fixtures. Additional format interoperability, wider accessibility/platform/scale work, new-body distribution, hosted verification and full-scope publication remain pending.",
